<!--
  A fixture of the UK Sanctions List, written from its schema (SanctionsListSchema-4.33.3.xsd, read
  on 2026-10-30) and its format guide (published 22 December 2025), with fictional names, and in
  the shape of the real file.

  Checked against the real file on 2026-10-31 (generated 2026-10-30): the connector read its 1,667
  entities with no error; IndividualEntityShip is Individual, Entity or Ship; NameType is Primary
  Name, Primary Name Variation or Alias, also written in other cases (Primary name, ALias), hence
  the comparison without regard to case; dates are dd/mm/yyyy; UNReferenceNumber appears only on
  designations the UN made (269 entities, two written QDE.).

  The paths the connector reads, from the XSD (every field an element):
    /Designations                                    root
    /Designations/DateGenerated                      the list's date (source version)
    /Designations/Designation                        one designation, repeated
      UniqueID, RegimeName, IndividualEntityShip, UNReferenceNumber, DateDesignated, LastUpdated
      Names/Name/Name1 … Name6, Names/Name/NameType
      Websites/Website
      EntityDetails/Entity/TypeOfEntities/TypeOfEntity
      EntityDetails/Entity/BusinessRegistrationNumbers/BusinessRegistrationNumber

  The shape of the real file, which the fixture keeps: the root declares the prefixes xsi and xsd
  and no default namespace; a designation lists its fields in the real order; RegimeName is the
  full title of the regulation; an entity's name is in Name6; UNReferenceNumber is there only on a
  designation the UN made, which DesignationSource then calls UN or UK|UN; a business registration
  number may hold two lines; a Website may be an address on a platform where many have pages, or an
  e-mail address. The fields the connector does not read are left out, except OFSIGroupID and
  DesignationSource. The XSD gives no date format, and the connector also reads an ISO 8601 day.
-->
